WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.425
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:03.880
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.600
The Kaibab Plateau is home
to one of the last ponderosa

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.830
pine forests in the southwest.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.960
It's a unique habitat, protected
by Grand Canyon National Park,

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.640
and a spectacle to behold.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.958
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.340
Less than 5% of the 6 million
annual visitors to the park

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.470
make it beyond the rim.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.781
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.360
For most, a trip to
a scenic overlook

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.260
is enough to get a taste of
the beauty in this magic place.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.599
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.750
But for those with a
sense of adventure,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.250
traveling into the heart of the
park can be quite the thrill.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.708
[WATER RUSHING]

00:01:04.684 --> 00:01:08.150
[SPLASHING]

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:14.360
A Grand Canyon rafting trip is
the adventure of a lifetime.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.840
It can take two weeks to
raft its entire length.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.420
Entrusting their
fate to the river,

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.210
paddlers navigate their
way through at least

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:33.180
80 big water rapids, including
the infamous Lava Falls.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.638
[WATER RUSHING]

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:55.660
The waters of the Colorado
are a rafters mecca--

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.005
but it's best not to fall in.

00:02:06.224 --> 00:02:08.160
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.680
The Grand Canyon
Pink Rattlesnake--

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.950
only found in this
region, it's perfectly

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.268
adapted to canyon life.

00:02:21.268 --> 00:02:24.600
[TONGUE FLICKING]

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.290
While the river is a
barrier to some, for him,

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.760
it's an opportunity.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.232
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.920
Swimming gives him
the freedom to search

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.195
for new hunting grounds.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.650
His ability to scour
more of the park

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.805
gives Grand Canyon its own
natural form of rodent control.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:13.450
Spring is a common season
to spot rattlesnakes.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.800
[MUSIC PLAYING]

